In article <1991Nov7.222435.1@jaguar.uofs.edu> cmj1@jaguar.uofs.edu writes:
>My Character ate a nymph, and now he's teleporting all over the place? I can't
>wear a ring of teleport control because I don't have one, nor do i dare free
>a finger for it! (I have polymorph and polymorph control) Is there/can I wish
>for and amulet of polymorph control? Or any other way i can rid myself of this?
     Unless you're a Wizard (in which case you gain intrinsic teleport control
at around 12th level), or unless you find and eat a tengu corpse, the only
useful thing I know of for this is the ring of teleport control.  (A gremlin
might zap your "teleporting" intrinsic, I guess, but it'd be just as likely to
zap something else that's useful.)

> Also, I got a genie to grant me a wish I typed '+3 stormbringer' and it said
>'never heard of it' (or something to that effect.) What's the deal? Did I do
>something wrong?

     When you wish for something, you have to phrase your wish pretty much
exactly as the item would be displayed in the inventory screen.  In this case,
your wish would be something like "a blessed +3 longsword named Stormbringer".
Of course, I'm not sure if you can wish for named items anymore.
